  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0038 database is a comprehensive system for managing user accounts, email verification, password resets, group permissions, content types, migrations, sessions, anonymous and user subscriptions, news comments, items, and votes. The accounts_customuser table stores information about each user, including their password, login history, and profile details, with a unique identifier and a foreign key referencing the accounts_invitation table for invitation tracking. The accounts_customuser_groups table links users to groups, while the accounts_customuser_user_permissions table assigns permissions to users. The accounts_emailverification table manages email verification requests, and the accounts_invitation table handles invitation codes and tracking. The accounts_passwordresetrequest table stores password reset requests. The auth_group table stores group information, and the auth_group_permissions table links groups to permissions. The auth_permission table contains permission details, and the django_admin_log table tracks administrative actions. The django_content_type table stores content type information, and the django_migrations table keeps track of database migrations. The django_session table stores user session data. The emaildigest_anonymoussubscription table stores anonymous subscription information, and the emaildigest_emaildigest table manages email digest settings. The emaildigest_emaildigest_stories table links email digests to news stories. The emaildigest_subscription table stores user subscription information, and the emaildigest_unsubscription table tracks unsubscribed users. The emaildigest_usersubscription table links users to subscriptions. The news_comment table stores comments on news items, and the news_item table stores news item details, including upvotes, downvotes, and comments. The news_story table stores news story information, and the news_vote table tracks user votes on news items.",
  "gold_question": "Pythonic News Platform\n\n 1) Background / Context\nPythonic News is an online community platform inspired by Hacker News, and it serves as a hub for Python enthusiasts. It is designed to allow members of the Python programming community to share and discuss news, articles, and projects related to Python. The platform is built using Python and Django and powers the website https://news.python.sc.\n\n 2) Objectives\n- To create a collaborative community for sharing Python-related content.\n- To facilitate discussions and engagement through a commenting system.\n- To highlight valuable content through a voting mechanism.\n- To organize content into categories, improving user navigation and content discovery.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n- Community Members: Python enthusiasts and developers who contribute and engage with the content.\n- Administrators: Oversee platform operations and manage user activities.\n- Developers: Maintain and improve the platform's functionality and user experience.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n- User Submissions: Members can submit links to Python-related content, encouraging collaboration and knowledge sharing.\n- Commenting System: Users can discuss, ask questions, and provide insights on submitted posts, fostering community engagement.\n- Voting Mechanism: Posts and comments can be upvoted or downvoted, promoting the most valuable content.\n- Content Categorization: Organizes content into categories for easier navigation and discovery.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Performance: The platform should efficiently handle a large number of users and content without performance degradation.\n- Usability: The user interface should be intuitive, enabling users to easily browse, submit, and engage with content.\n- Security: Implement secure authentication and authorization mechanisms to protect user data and platform integrity.\n- Scalability: The infrastructure should support growth in user base and functionality without significant changes to the existing system.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0038.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0038\nCREATE TABLE `accounts_customuser` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `login_history` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `profile_details` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `invitation_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `accounts_customuser_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`invitation_id`) REFERENCES `accounts_invitation` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `accounts_customuser_groups` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `group_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `group_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `accounts_customuser_groups_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `accounts_customuser` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `accounts_customuser_groups_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`group_id`) REFERENCES `auth_group` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `accounts_customuser_user_permissions` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `permission_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `permission_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `accounts_customuser_user_permissions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `accounts_customuser` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `accounts_customuser_user_permissions_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`permission_id`) REFERENCES `auth_permission` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `accounts_emailverification` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `verification_code` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `accounts_emailverification_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `accounts_customuser` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `accounts_invitation` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `invitation_code` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `accounts_passwordresetrequest` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `reset_token` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `accounts_passwordresetrequest_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `accounts_customuser` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `auth_group` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `auth_group_permissions` (\n  `group_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `permission_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`group_id`, `permission_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `auth_group_permissions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`group_id`) REFERENCES `auth_group` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `auth_group_permissions_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`permission_id`) REFERENCES `auth_permission` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `auth_permission` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `codename` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `django_admin_log` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `action_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content_type_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `object_id` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `object_repr` varchar(200) NOT NULL,\n  `action_flag` smallint(6) NOT NULL,\n  `change_message` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `django_admin_log_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `accounts_customuser` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `django_admin_log_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`content_type_id`) REFERENCES `django_content_type` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `django_content_type` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `app_label` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `model` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `django_migrations` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `app` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `applied` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `django_session` (\n  `session_key` char(40) NOT NULL,\n  `session_data` text NOT NULL,\n  `expire_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`session_key`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `emaildigest_anonymoussubscription` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `emaildigest_emaildigest` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `settings` text NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `emaildigest_emaildigest_stories` (\n  `digest_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`digest_id`, `story_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `emaildigest_emaildigest_stories_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`digest_id`) REFERENCES `emaildigest_emaildigest` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `emaildigest_emaildigest_stories_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`story_id`) REFERENCES `news_story` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `emaildigest_subscription` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `emaildigest_subscription_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `accounts_customuser` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `emaildigest_unsubscription` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `emaildigest_unsubscription_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `accounts_customuser` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `emaildigest_usersubscription` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `subscription_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `subscription_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `emaildigest_usersubscription_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `accounts_customuser` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `emaildigest_usersubscription_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`subscription_id`) REFERENCES `emaildigest_subscription` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `news_comment` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `item_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `comment` text NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `news_comment_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`item_id`) REFERENCES `news_item` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `news_comment_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `accounts_customuser` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `news_item` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `upvotes` int(11) DEFAULT 0,\n  `downvotes` int(11) DEFAULT 0,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `news_story` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `news_vote` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `item_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `vote_type` enum('upvote', 'downvote') NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `news_vote_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`item_id`) REFERENCES `news_item` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `news_vote_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `accounts_customuser` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
